            <ArticleTitle>An association of central post-stroke pain and thalamic hand.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>120-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thalamic hand is one of the clinical expressions of the painful thalamic syndrome. This paper relates on a case of a patient with a syndrome of central post-stroke and supra-thalamic pain who also presents a thalamic hand. The authors emphasize the notion that in the syndrome of central post-stroke pain a direct or indirect (infra or supra)-thalamic lesion seems to be an essential element for the genesis of central pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
